  by: agent  # f27a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f27a
  clock: 7  # f27a
  nonce: f27a  # f27a
  message: "Fixed in the PR cited above (merged; dev 69a06a23fd). Behavioral evidence, re-running the item's own filed repro on dev (src/main.ts = `import { u } from \"./util.js\"`, src/util.js = `export function u()`; `hypergumbo run`): exactly ONE util.js file node, `javascript:src/util.js:1-1:file:file`. No `typescript:src/util.js` phantom. `imports typescript:src/main.ts -> javascript:src/util.js` and `module_exports javascript:src/util.js -> ...:u:function` both hang off the real node.\nAsset case (copy of nextjs test/integration/image-optimizer/app): 15 image file nodes, all language=None, discovery_language=javascript (before the fix: language=javascript).\nProduction-path test TestImportTargetCarriesItsOwnLanguage: util.js minted as javascript, style.css reuses the css analyzer node, logo.png has language None / discovery typescript. It was red on the old code (typescript != javascript). smart-test: 3485 passed, changed sources at 100% coverage.\nAnalogue sweep over make_file_id callers: no other producer mints a target in the importer's language (vue_component mints only .vue as vue; lean only .lean; html script_src was fixed by WI-majov).\nNOT EXAMINED: the repro output still carries the analyzer's unresolved edge `imports typescript:src/main.ts -> typescript:./util.js:0-0:module:external_symbol` beside the resolved one. I did not check whether that predates this change or whether it is intended."  # f27a
